<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jagir</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A jagir was an assignment of land revenue to an official or military commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-asia">South Asia</a>, typically in return for service. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> jagirs supported the mansabdars, and were usually transferable rather than hereditary. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> also used jagirs to reward its chiefs and officers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jagir.jpg" alt="Jagir" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Maratha school · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maratha_darbar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
